# Docs and Release Workflow Standards

- Keep roadmap/checklist docs actionable and ordered; prefer checklists for release-critical steps.
- When steps reference code changes, include exact paths and keep links current.
- Update related docs together (for example publish roadmap + production checklist) when behavior changes.
- Distinguish clearly between required pre-release items and post-launch improvements.
- Record known issues with impact and mitigation, not just symptoms.
- Use concise language and avoid duplicate sections that can drift over time.

## Quick Checks

- Versioned/release instructions still match current commands and artifact paths.
- Privacy, support, and store metadata references point to the canonical source in code/docs.
